TESTDATA["pet4-t4"] = {"title":"Cambridge PET 4 · Test 4","format":"2010","reading":[{"part":1,"items":[{"n":1,"text":"If red light shows, your drink is unavailable – please make another choice","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","q":"","options":["The red light goes on if the drinks machine is out of order.","If the red light shows, you must wait before you decide on a drink.","If the red light is on, you must choose a different drink."],"answer":"C"},{"n":2,"text":"Do not use this medicine for more than seven days without your doctor's advice","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","q":"","options":["Contact your doctor if you wish to continue using this medicine after one week.","Doctors can only supply enough medicine for one week at a time.","You cannot keep this medicine for more than seven days."],"answer":"A"},{"n":3,"text":"From: Sunflowers Health Club\nTo: All Members   Sent 15 April\nSubject: Special Offer\nIntroduce a friend to this club and receive free exercise equipment! This offer is open to existing members; your friend must pay full 12-month fee.","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","q":"","options":["Sunflowers is selling exercise equipment to members at a special price.","You will qualify for a gift if you persuade a friend to join Sunflowers.","Your annual fee for Sunflowers Health Club must be paid now."],"answer":"B"},{"n":4,"text":"Please don't park within 3 metres of this vehicle – space needed for unloading","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","q":"","options":["You should not park near here because it is an exit for vehicles.","This parking space is reserved for the vehicle's owner.","You are requested not to park any closer than 3 metres to this vehicle."],"answer":"C"},{"n":5,"text":"This tower's in wonderful green stone, with 497 steps – stupidly, I climbed to the top! The view's supposed to be brilliant but yesterday was cloudy.\nKenny","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","q":"What did Kenny like about the tower?","options":["the view it gave from the top","the material used to build it","the number of steps it has"],"answer":"B"}]},{"part":2,"people":[{"n":6,"name":"David","text":"David enjoys walking but he has injured his knee and cannot climb up hills. He would like to spend a couple of hours on a quiet walk with well-marked paths.","answer":"C"},{"n":7,"name":"Luigi","text":"Luigi likes to get as much exercise as possible and particularly likes climbing steep hills to get a good view. He wants to do a walk that is difficult and offers a range of scenery.","answer":"E"},{"n":8,"name":"Yannis","text":"Yannis has two sons of 8 and 10. He would like to take them to see some animals in the countryside. He wants to be able to buy some refreshments.","answer":"D"},{"n":9,"name":"Amanda","text":"Amanda has had an operation and needs plenty of fresh air to help her recover. She wants to find a short, quiet walk with a beautiful place to visit on the route.","answer":"H"},{"n":10,"name":"Claudia","text":"Claudia's grandparents are staying with her. They are very fit and enjoy walking. They would like to visit some of the local villages and need a clearly-marked route so they don't lose their way.","answer":"B"}],"texts":[{"letter":"A","title":"MILL LANE","text":"You'll see lots of animals on this walk, because there is nothing to disturb them. Walkers often say they meet no-one. There are places where you can join or finish the walk but these are not well signposted and it is easy to get lost."},{"letter":"B","title":"SEA PATH","text":"This walk starts at the village of Nye Flats and the excellent signposts lead you through local streets, fields and pretty neighbouring villages. Although it will take you half a day, there are no hills at all. You can breathe the sea air and enjoy watching traditional life in busy villages."},{"letter":"C","title":"CUTTERS WAY","text":"This walk can take anything from 30 minutes to two hours. It's not a good walk for hill-lovers as the ground is completely flat, but it has good signposts and simple facilities for the hungry or thirsty walker. A few places or things to see would improve this walk, which can be a little dull."},{"letter":"D","title":"PADDOCK WAY","text":"This is really a short track across a working farm. There are plenty of chickens and sheep to see, and the farmer has turned some of the buildings into an educational centre with a café. Not a walk for those who like peace and quiet, but good fun."},{"letter":"E","title":"HURDLES","text":"This is a route for the experienced walker. It crosses two rivers and includes hills of up to 500 metres, from which you can see the sea. There are several rocky paths that are unsuitable for children or older people, and there are no shops so take plenty of water."},{"letter":"F","title":"NEVERLAND","text":"This is a walk to take if you have a whole day to spare and want to escape from other people. It follows a narrow track which is clearly marked and has different routes for different types of walker. There are hills to climb but views are limited because of thick forest."},{"letter":"G","title":"OVERHILL","text":"This sounds like a difficult walk but it's really easy, although it could be better signposted. If you're a local person, you're almost certain to meet someone you know on the walk. It's a couple of kilometres outside the village of Overhill, with fields full of rabbits!"},{"letter":"H","title":"GOLD-DIGGERS END","text":"You won't find any gold on this peaceful walk, but you will find plenty of other things to see including a lovely garden which is open to the public. It's a half-hour walk with a couple of small cafés on the way."}]},{"part":3,"title":"GODDINGTON THEATRE","text":"The Goddington Theatre Ticket Office is open from 12 noon until 4 p.m. Monday to Friday, and for half an hour in the evening before the advertised start time of each performance.\n\nTelephone bookings\n• Your tickets are held at the Ticket Office for you to collect or, if you prefer, a charge of 35p is made to post them to you. No extra charge is made for bookings by credit card.\n• Reservations are held for up to four days, allowing time to call in to pay for the tickets or to send payments in the post.\n\nPostal bookings\n• You can write to the Ticket Office requesting tickets, or to confirm a reservation.\n\nInformation for the disabled\n• The theatre has space for up to five wheelchairs at a performance, as the seats in positions 12–16 of row A can be removed.\n• If you have difficulty with stairs, please let us know when booking.\n\nWhere to find Goddington Theatre\nGoddington Theatre can be found within the Goddington University site, next to the car park, which is available for public use after 5 p.m. on weekdays and all day at weekends.\n\nIf travelling by car\nComing from the south end of Princes Street, you will see the library on your right. The next building on your right is Goddington University – there is a pedestrian crossing outside the front entrance. Take the next turning on the right after the crossing (into Broad Street) which takes you along the side of Goddington University – then first right into the car park. Drive up to the car park gate straight ahead of you, stopping as close as possible to the orange machine. Put a £1 coin in the machine and the gate will rise. (Note: Do not try to put a coin in the machine by getting out of your car – it is likely that by the time you get back in your car the gate will already be closed again!) Other car parks are shown on the map. There is an hourly charge. You may find a free parking place on one of the side streets.\n\nIf travelling by train\nYou will need to allow 30 minutes to walk from the station. Taxis are available from the front of the station.\n\nIf travelling by bus/coach\nThe University is a 5 to 10-minute walk from the main bus station.\n\nTaxis\nWhen ordering a taxi from the theatre, ask to be picked up at the bottom of North Street. Taxis will not come into the car park because of the entrance charge.","items":[{"n":11,"q":"If a performance begins at 8 p.m., the Goddington Theatre Ticket Office re-opens at 7.30 that evening.","answer":"A"},{"n":12,"q":"Bookings by credit card cost more.","answer":"B"},{"n":13,"q":"You must pay for tickets when you reserve them.","answer":"B"},{"n":14,"q":"Wheelchairs are allowed in front of row A.","answer":"B"},{"n":15,"q":"The public can use the university car park at certain times only.","answer":"A"},{"n":16,"q":"The university is on the same side of the road as the library.","answer":"A"},{"n":17,"q":"The car park is in front of the university building.","answer":"B"},{"n":18,"q":"You need to drive away quickly after putting your money in the car park machine.","answer":"A"},{"n":19,"q":"The railway station is nearer the university than the bus station.","answer":"B"},{"n":20,"q":"Taxi drivers refuse to pick up customers inside the car park.","answer":"A"}]},{"part":4,"title":"","text":"Orbis is an organisation which helps blind people everywhere. It has built an eye hospital inside an aeroplane and flown it all over the world with an international medical team. Samantha Graham, a fourteen-year-old schoolgirl from England, went with the plane to Mongolia. Samantha tells the story of Eukhtuul, a young Mongolian girl.\n\n'Last year, when Eukhtuul was walking home from school, she was attacked by boys with sticks and her eyes were badly damaged. Dr Duffey, an Orbis doctor, said that without an operation she would never see again. I thought about all the everyday things I do that she couldn't, things like reading schoolbooks, watching television, seeing friends, and I realised how lucky I am.'\n\n'The Orbis team agreed to operate on Eukhtuul and I was allowed to watch, together with some Mongolian medical students. I prayed the operation would be successful. The next day I waited nervously with Eukhtuul while Dr Duffey removed her bandages. \"In six months your sight will be back to normal,\" he said. Eukhtuul smiled, her mother cried, and I had to wipe away some tears, too!'\n\n'Now Eukhtuul wants to study hard to become a doctor. Her whole future has changed, thanks to a simple operation. We should all think more about how much our sight means to us.'","items":[{"n":21,"q":"What is the writer's main purpose in writing this text?","options":["to describe a dangerous trip","to report a patient's cure","to explain how sight can be lost","to warn against playing with sticks"],"answer":"B"},{"n":22,"q":"What can a reader learn about in this text?","options":["the life of schoolchildren in Mongolia","the difficulties for blind travellers","the international work of some eye doctors","the best way of studying medicine"],"answer":"C"},{"n":23,"q":"After meeting Eukhtuul, Samantha felt","options":["grateful for her own sight.","proud of the doctor's skill.","surprised by Eukhtuul's courage.","angry about Eukhtuul's experience."],"answer":"A"},{"n":24,"q":"What is the result of Eukhtuul's operation?","options":["She can already see perfectly again.","After some time she will see as well as before.","She can see better but will never have normal eyes.","Before she recovers, she will need another operation."],"answer":"B"},{"n":25,"q":"Which is the postcard Samantha wrote to an English friend?","options":["I've visited a Mongolian hospital and watched local doctors do an operation.","You may have to fly a long way to have the operation you need, but the journey will be worth it.","I'm staying with my friend Eukhtuul, while I'm sightseeing in Mongolia.","Make sure you take care of your eyes because they're more valuable than you realise!"],"answer":"D"}]},{"part":5,"title":"The History of Film","text":"The world's first film was shown in 1895 (0) ……… (by) two French brothers, Louis and Auguste Lumière. Although it only [26] of short, simple scenes, people loved it and films have [27] popular ever since. The first films were silent, with titles on the screen to [28] the story.\nSoon the public had [29] favourite actors and actresses and, in this [30], the first film stars appeared. In 1927, the first 'talkie', a film with sound, was shown and from then on, the public [31] only accept this kind of film.\nFurther improvements continued, particularly in America, [32] produced 95% of all films. With the arrival of television in the 1950s, [33] people went to see films, but in [34] years cinema audiences have grown again. More countries have started to produce films that influence film-making and there are currently [35] national film industries.","gaps":{"26":{"options":["consisted","contained","belonged","held"],"answer":"A"},"27":{"options":["gone","been","made","kept"],"answer":"B"},"28":{"options":["join","read","explain","perform"],"answer":"C"},"29":{"options":["your","his","our","their"],"answer":"D"},"30":{"options":["reason","way","method","result"],"answer":"B"},"31":{"options":["should","would","might","will"],"answer":"B"},"32":{"options":["who","where","when","which"],"answer":"D"},"33":{"options":["other","each","fewer","any"],"answer":"C"},"34":{"options":["recent","now","modern","present"],"answer":"A"},"35":{"options":["many","lots","much","plenty"],"answer":"A"}}}],"writing":[{"part":1,"title":"Here are some sentences about visiting a zoo.","items":[{"n":1,"first":"We had a map but it was difficult to find the zoo.","before":"Although we had a map, we","after":"find the zoo easily.","answers":["couldn't","could not","didn't","did not"]},{"n":2,"first":"The car park was outside the main entrance.","before":"There was somewhere","after":"outside the main entrance.","answers":["to park"]},{"n":3,"first":"We wore sun hats because it was very hot.","before":"It was","after":"that we wore sun hats.","answers":["so very hot","so hot","so very sunny","so sunny"]},{"n":4,"first":"Maria suggested going to see the monkeys.","before":"Maria said, 'Why don't we","after":"the monkeys?'","answers":["go to see","go and see"]},{"n":5,"first":"The elephants were my favourite animals.","before":"I liked the elephants","after":"any other animal.","answers":["more than","better than"]}]},{"part":2,"items":[{"n":6,"kind":"message","task":"Some English friends are going to visit your capital city and have asked you to recommend a hotel there.\n\nWrite an email to your friends. In your email, you should\n• say which hotel your friends should book\n• explain why you are recommending the hotel\n• suggest what they could do near the hotel.\n\nWrite 35–45 words on your answer sheet.","points":["suggerire quale hotel prenotare","spiegare perché lo consiglia","suggerire che cosa possono fare vicino all'hotel"]}]},{"part":3,"items":[{"n":7,"kind":"story","task":"You have to write a story for your English homework.\nYour story must have this title:\n\nThe empty house\n\nWrite your story in about 100 words on your answer sheet."},{"n":8,"kind":"letter","task":"This is part of a letter you receive from an English-speaking friend.\n\n'I want to earn some money at the weekends, so I'm looking for a part-time job in a café or a shop. Which do you think would be more fun? Write soon – I need your advice!'\n\nNow write a letter giving your friend some advice.\nWrite your letter in about 100 words on your answer sheet."}]}],"listening":[{"part":1,"audio":"audio/pet4-t4-l1.mp3","items":[{"n":1,"q":"Where will the woman go first after work?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"B"},{"n":2,"q":"What can festival visitors see every day?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"B"},{"n":3,"q":"What souvenir will the boy's mother bring?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"C"},{"n":4,"q":"What time is the woman's hair appointment?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"A"},{"n":5,"q":"Where's the TV guide?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"C"},{"n":6,"q":"What does the man decide to take Tracy?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"B"},{"n":7,"q":"Which sport has the man just started?","img":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["","",""],"answer":"C"}],"example":"img/pet4-t4-l1-ex.jpg"},{"part":2,"intro":"You will hear a man called John Dalin talking about the travel programmes he makes for television.","audio":"audio/pet4-t4-l2.mp3","items":[{"n":8,"q":"For his most recent television programme, John","options":["drove from the North to the South Pole.","filmed relaxing beach holidays.","went to the Pacific Ocean for a year."],"answer":"C"},{"n":9,"q":"John is giving up very long trips because","options":["he's too old now.","he's been everywhere.","they're too tiring."],"answer":"C"},{"n":10,"q":"John says his next television series might be about","options":["farms in Scotland.","old ruins in Wales.","cycling tours in France."],"answer":"B"},{"n":11,"q":"John wants to encourage other people to","options":["be brave about travelling to new places.","lose their fear of flying.","make more trips alone."],"answer":"A"},{"n":12,"q":"Why does John want to spend more time near home?","options":["His family might need him.","His wife misses him.","He has very young children."],"answer":"A"},{"n":13,"q":"John has already written some","options":["newspaper articles.","travel books.","poems."],"answer":"B"}]},{"part":3,"intro":"You will hear a woman talking on the radio about an exhibition of food and cooking.","audio":"audio/pet4-t4-l3.mp3","notes":"The Good Food Show\nat the Capital Exhibition Centre\nAt the show, you can\n• buy Jane Adams' new book about making [14]\n• get advice about buying [15]\n• watch how to cook a lunch just with [16]\n• learn how to make a dessert in less than [17]\n• taste food from many different countries – the food from [18] is specially recommended.\nThe show finishes on [19].","answers":{"14":["cakes"],"15":["fresh fish","fish"],"16":["vegetables"],"17":["15 minutes","fifteen minutes","15","fifteen"],"18":["Canada"],"19":["23 March","23rd March","March 23","March 23rd","23rd of March"]}},{"part":4,"intro":"You will hear a conversation between a teenage girl called Anna and her father about a party.","audio":"audio/pet4-t4-l4.mp3","items":[{"n":20,"q":"Anna begins by asking her father to collect her from the party.","answer":"B"},{"n":21,"q":"The party is to celebrate Tom's birthday.","answer":"B"},{"n":22,"q":"Some of Tom's relations will be at the party.","answer":"A"},{"n":23,"q":"Anna's father is worried about her attending the party.","answer":"B"},{"n":24,"q":"Anna's father will take them to the party before the film starts.","answer":"B"},{"n":25,"q":"Anna's father insists that she leaves the party at 12.00.","answer":"A"}]}]};
